# The atoms of the language's carrier actor contract (transport design 6.2) that BEES spells or prints: the reasons a
# link ends with (spelled in audit lines through bees_atoms@spelling) and the tags of dangerous_bees_net's own actor messages.
# The contract's message tags themselves (:open, :tx, :credit, :close, :link_up, :accepted, :rx, :tx_credit, :tx_failed,
# :link_down) are written as literals where the carrier is spoken, as the language's own programs write them; they are
# listed here so that every node program holds them in its atom table.
open
tx
credit
close
link_up
accepted
rx
tx_credit
tx_failed
link_down
closed
reset
timeout
fault
no_credit
bees
car
who
